{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles and Frankie Valli feel like natural next choices because I want familiar older songs, much like the classic rock and mid-sixties collections I have chosen before.",
    "Neil Diamond and Bread fit the gentle melodies I enjoy in Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie; that musical connection matters more to me than simply being a greatest-hits collection."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In The Lonely Hour and 25 lean toward contemporary pop and ballads when I am more interested in revisiting older hits. Having listened to Born This Way does not mean newer pop is my main interest now.",
    "Number One Hits and The Greatest Hits Collection do not give me enough information about whose music I would hear, so I cannot connect them to the songs and artists I enjoy."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selections seem to treat a greatest-hits title as enough evidence of a match, but I choose collections for the artists and music they contain.",
    "My occasional newer pop and vocal-album choices seem to carry too much weight compared with my repeated interest in older rock, folk, and pop collections."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated choices of older compilations suggest that familiar songs from those eras are especially appealing to me right now.",
    "A possible fit is not always something I would choose today: To Be Loved connects with Cheek to Cheek, and Santana fits my classic rock interest, but I would reach for Eagles or Frankie Valli first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in familiar hits, but sometimes stretch that into any hit collection or newer vocal album without enough connection to the older music I want now."
}"}
